---
import { site } from '../../site.config';
---
<section id="vllm">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>vLLM</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a maintainer of <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm">vLLM</a>, mostly in the
      compilation stack: <code>torch.compile</code> integration, fusion passes, and CUDA graphs.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <b>Need a PR reviewed?</b> Ping me in the <a href="#">vLLM Slack</a> — the
        <code>#feat-torch-compile</code> channel is better than a DM, and better still is a link to
        the PR with one sentence on what it changes and how you tested it. I don't reliably see
        GitHub mentions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="quiet">
      I take a small number of consulting engagements on vLLM performance — compilation, fusion, and
      inference throughput. <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email me</a> if that's useful to your
      team.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
